{
  "name": "Supreme Healing",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell, you instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 hit points to a creature, you restore 12.</p><p>If the healing formula of the spell involves a static number (beside your spellcasting ability modifier), you increase that number by half, rounded down.</p>",
